1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,220
This is the implementation demo for journey two.

2
00:00:03,220 --> 00:00:07,590
It is the real admin application and API running on this machine,

3
00:00:07,590 --> 00:00:11,760
with synthetic people and a local mailbox that sends no email.

4
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:16,930
It shows how an administrator decides which mechanics and body shops can take

5
00:00:16,930 --> 00:00:17,740
inspections.

6
00:00:18,890 --> 00:00:22,670
The administrator signs in and lands on the provider list.

7
00:00:22,670 --> 00:00:26,390
Each provider shows a kind, licence, location and status.

8
00:00:26,390 --> 00:00:29,400
The two seeded providers are already approved.

9
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:33,120
Providers who register themselves arrive here as pending.

10
00:00:34,270 --> 00:00:37,200
To add a provider, open the onboard dialog.

11
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:42,800
With a bad email and nothing else filled in, the dialog lists exactly what to fix.

12
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:44,300
Now a valid body shop.

13
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:48,880
It is added as pending, which means it cannot take inspections yet,

14
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:52,220
and it is emailed a link to set its own password.

15
00:00:53,370 --> 00:00:58,660
Approving asks for confirmation, then the shop shows as approved and can take

16
00:00:58,660 --> 00:00:59,480
inspections.

17
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:04,090
Deactivating also asks, and the safe choice, cancel, has the focus.

18
00:01:04,090 --> 00:01:09,240
The dialog explains that inspections already booked stay with the provider,

19
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:10,890
and only new work stops.

20
00:01:10,890 --> 00:01:14,320
After deactivating, the shop shows as deactivated,

21
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:16,870
and one more approval brings it back.

22
00:01:18,020 --> 00:01:20,630
Only administrators can do any of this.

23
00:01:20,630 --> 00:01:25,710
A buyer who signs in to the admin app is told it is for administrators only,

24
00:01:25,710 --> 00:01:29,990
and the API refuses the same requests with a forbidden response.

25
00:01:31,140 --> 00:01:32,950
Here is what to remember.

26
00:01:32,950 --> 00:01:34,980
New providers start pending.

27
00:01:34,980 --> 00:01:38,020
Approval lets a provider take inspections,

28
00:01:38,020 --> 00:01:42,860
and deactivation stops new work without touching existing bookings.

29
00:01:42,860 --> 00:01:47,420
Every change is confirmed, and only administrators can make it.

30
00:01:47,420 --> 00:01:50,390
Next, journey three: manage availability.
